---
import PrimerChat from "../PrimerChat.astro";
import { archiveAi } from "../../../lib/archive-ai";
import { proveIt } from "../../../lib/archive";
import { spell } from "../../../lib/cases";

const card = archiveAi["prove-it"];
const { boxScores, withOvertime } = proveIt.slots.replay;
const boxes = spell(boxScores);
const others = spell(boxScores - withOvertime);
const fresh = spell(proveIt.slots.stale.schedulesFresh);

const oakJan = { published: 40, secondIds: 3 };
const oakJanReplayed = oakJan.published - oakJan.secondIds;
type Row = { output: string; fp: string; published: number; replayed: number | null; verdict: string; rest: string; tone: string };
const rows: Row[] = [
  { output: "Oak Pantry, January", fp: "Changed. Its inputs went through the corrected importer.", published: oakJan.published, replayed: oakJanReplayed, verdict: "Republish", rest: "after approval.", tone: "is-bad" },
  { output: "Oak Pantry, February", fp: "Changed. Its inputs went through the same importer.", published: 42, replayed: 42, verdict: "Keep", rest: "the published count. Record the verified replay internally.", tone: "is-ok" },
  { output: "Maple Pantry, January", fp: "Matched. Its inputs came through a separate importer.", published: 25, replayed: null, verdict: "Leave", rest: "the publication alone. Skip replay.", tone: "is-quiet" },
];
const ids = Array.from({ length: oakJan.published }, (_, i) => i >= oakJan.published - oakJan.secondIds);

const agentPrompt = `Fix the duplicate-household counting bug and prepare a correction to the
food bank network's published monthly pantry counts. A household should
count once per pantry per month, even if it visited more than once.

For each published pantry-month, locate its archived input snapshot and
saved publication fingerprint. Compute the expected fingerprint using
that same snapshot and the corrected versions of the processing steps,
rules, and configuration that the output actually depends on. Compare
the fingerprints to identify stale outputs. Flag missing snapshots or
incomplete dependency records as unresolved.

Replay stale outputs in staging using the archived inputs. Include any
downstream publications that depend on them. Compare the replayed
published values with the originals and verify the reason for each
difference. Stage replacements only for outputs whose published values
changed. Record successful replays with unchanged values internally.
Leave outputs with verified matching fingerprints alone.

For example, Oak Pantry's January count might change from ${oakJan.published} to ${oakJanReplayed}
after ${oakJan.secondIds} duplicate household IDs are resolved. If Oak's February
count replays from 42 to 42, keep its published count. If Maple's
January fingerprint matches because it used a separate importer, skip
its replay. Verify the actual results independently of these examples.

Before republishing, report which outputs were replayed, skipped, or
unresolved and why. Include the old and new values for every proposed
correction, the validation performed, any affected downstream
publications, and a draft correction note naming the affected pantry
and month, the old and new counts, and the cause.

Stop after delivering the report and staged replacements. Wait for
explicit approval before republishing or sending the correction note.`;

const briefParas = agentPrompt.split(/\n\n/).map((para) => para.replace(/\s*\n\s*/g, " "));

const checks = [
  ["Oak's February", "Why is Oak's February count replayed even though its published value stays at 42?"],
  ["Skipping Maple", "What evidence lets the agent skip Maple's January replay, and what should it do if that evidence is missing?"],
  ["Already used", "What should the correction note tell someone who already used Oak's January count in a report?"],
];
---

<PrimerChat
  prompt={card.prompt}
  module="Module 2"
  back="../02-archive/#prove-it-slots"
  about="This is a reply an AI assistant gave to Module 2's recovery-plan study prompt, lightly edited. Send the same prompt yourself and you will get a different reply."
  turn={`In a live chat, you would answer those three questions and the assistant would review your reasoning. To try that, copy the prompt into your own AI assistant. Then go back to Part 8 and ${card.returnTask.replace("Then come back and ", "")}`}
>
  <h2 class="pr-title">From recovery plan to agent prompt</h2>
  <p>Use the fingerprint to decide <strong>what to replay</strong>, then compare the replayed numbers with the published numbers to decide <strong>what to republish</strong>.</p>
  <p class="pr-pull">An output can need replay even if its numbers turn out to be correct.</p>

  <h2>1. One example</h2>
  <p>A food bank network publishes monthly counts of distinct households served by each pantry. Months after publication, it finds that an importer could assign a second ID to a household that returned during the same month.</p>
  <figure class="pr-card">
    <p class="pr-label">Oak Pantry, January: what the published count counted</p>
    <ul class="pa-ids" role="img" aria-label={`${oakJan.published} household IDs, ${oakJan.secondIds} of them second IDs for households that returned, so ${oakJanReplayed} distinct households.`}>
      {ids.map((second) => <li class:list={{ "is-second": second }}></li>)}
    </ul>
    <p class="pa-ids-key"><span><i></i>{oakJanReplayed} households</span><span><i class="is-second"></i>{oakJan.secondIds} second IDs for returning households</span></p>
    <figcaption>The published count was {oakJan.published} IDs. Counting each household once gives {oakJan.published} − {oakJan.secondIds} = {oakJanReplayed}.</figcaption>
  </figure>
  <p>Each published pantry-month has a saved fingerprint built from its archived input snapshot, the processing steps it uses, and the rules and configuration for those steps. The agent computes the expected fingerprint using the <strong>same archived inputs</strong> and the corrected processing steps. It compares that fingerprint with the one saved at publication.</p>
  <figure class="pr-card pa-plan">
    <p class="pr-label">Three published outputs</p>
    <label class="pa-reveal"><input type="checkbox" /> <span>Decide what to replay from the fingerprints, then show the replay and the reply's actions</span></label>
    <div class="pr-scroll">
      <table class="pr-table">
        <thead><tr><th scope="col">Published output</th><th scope="col">Fingerprint comparison</th><th scope="col">Published → replayed</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>{rows.map((r) => (
          <tr>
            <th scope="row">{r.output}</th>
            <td>{r.fp}</td>
            <td class="pa-num"><span class="pa-act">{r.published} → {r.replayed ?? "—"}</span><span class="pa-act-hidden">{r.published} → ?</span></td>
            <td><span class="pa-act"><span class:list={["pr-chip", r.tone]}>{r.verdict}</span> {r.rest}</span><span class="pa-act-hidden">Your call</span></td>
          </tr>
        ))}</tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </figure>
  <p>Oak's February count shows why the fingerprint is a replay trigger. The agent checks every output that depended on the affected importer, even when there is no known duplicate in that month. It also checks downstream publications that depend on those counts.</p>

  <h2>2. Correction note</h2>
  <blockquote class="pa-note">
    <p>We corrected Oak Pantry's January count of distinct households served from {oakJan.published} to {oakJanReplayed}. The original import assigned a second ID to {spell(oakJan.secondIds)} returning households, so each was counted twice. The revised count removes those duplicates. Please use {oakJanReplayed} in reports or analyses that cite Oak Pantry's January count.</p>
  </blockquote>

  <h2>3. Prompt to give the coding agent</h2>
  <figure class="pr-card pa-brief">
    <p class="pr-label">Prompt</p>
    {briefParas.map((para) => <p>{para}</p>)}
  </figure>
  <aside class="pr-course" aria-label="Course note">
    <p class="pr-label">Course note</p>
    <p>The reply's fingerprint covers a whole pantry-month: its input snapshot, steps, rules and configuration. In this course a fingerprint covers one parser's code and config, and each parsed file also keeps the content hash of the page it read. Either way, a difference marks the output stale, and the replay, not the fingerprint, decides what to republish.</p>
    <p>In Part 8 the box-score parser's fingerprint changed, so all {boxes} parsed Alder Ridge box scores are stale, like every Oak month that went through the importer. The {fresh} schedules come through their own parser and stay fresh, like Maple. The other {others} box scores are Oak's February: replayed, unchanged, nothing to republish. Part 8's third slot asks the reply's Maple question of the match detail and of the standings: did the bug ever reach it?</p>
  </aside>

  <h2>4. Check your understanding</h2>
  <ol class="pr-checks">{checks.map(([name, q]) => <li><b>{name}</b><span>{q}</span></li>)}</ol>
</PrimerChat>

<style>
  .pa-ids { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(10, 1fr); gap: 0.3rem; max-width: 22rem; margin: 0 0 0.6rem; padding: 0; list-style: none; }
  .pa-ids li { aspect-ratio: 1; border-radius: 4px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pr-green) 55%, transparent); }
  .pa-ids li.is-second { border: 1.5px dashed var(--pr-red); background: transparent; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-ids-key { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 0.3rem 1rem; margin: 0 0 0.2rem; color: var(--tl-muted); font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .pa-ids-key span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.4rem; }
  .pa-ids-key i { width: 0.8rem; height: 0.8rem; border-radius: 3px; background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--pr-green) 55%, transparent); }
  .pa-ids-key i.is-second { border: 1.5px dashed var(--pr-red); background: transparent; }
  .pa-plan :global(.pr-chip.is-quiet) { border: 1px solid var(--tl-line); background: transparent; color: var(--tl-muted); }
  .pa-num { white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  .pa-act-hidden { color: var(--tl-muted); font-style: italic; }
  .pa-plan:not(:has(.pa-reveal input:checked)) .pa-act { display: none; }
  .pa-plan:has(.pa-reveal input:checked) .pa-act-hidden { display: none; }
  .pa-reveal { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.45rem; min-height: 40px; margin: 0 0 0.4rem; font-size: 0.88rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .pa-reveal input { width: 1.1rem; height: 1.1rem; accent-color: var(--pr-ai); }
  .pa-note { margin: 0 0 1rem; padding: 0.7rem 0.95rem; border: 1px solid var(--tl-line); border-left: 4px solid var(--pr-yellow); border-radius: 8px; background: var(--tl-card); font-style: normal; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-note p:last-child { margin: 0; }
  .pa-brief { border-left: 3px solid var(--pr-ai); }
  :global(.pr) .pa-brief p:not(.pr-label) { margin: 0 0 0.6rem; font-size: 0.92rem; }
  :global(.pr) .pa-brief p:last-child { margin: 0; }
</style>
